{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1779386137,"nonce":"bAxIef13B16Vh1eetC7TgMIoc9o=","title":"Provider depth: eval/analysis/report manifests, artifacts, and actions","message":"## Purpose\n\nConcrete provider-depth child from `a3e46d5` for the remaining Feedbax provider/manifest contract work after the initial provider MVP, schema contract, and Studio vertical-slice foundations.\n\nThe goal is to make Feedbax provider outputs deep enough that Studio, scripts, agents, and Mandible can operate over the same durable records without hardcoding Feedbax internals or relying on UI-local metadata.\n\n## Scope\n\nImplement the next provider/manifest depth slice across `c6c6da0`, `f68cf66`, and `e33f487`.\n\nRequired work areas:\n\n- first-class `EvaluationRunManifest`, `AnalysisRunManifest`, and `ReportManifest` support, not only training-run manifests;\n- artifact refs for eval/analysis/report products, including trajectory datasets, tables, figures, logs, report bundles, checkpoints, and config/spec snapshots;\n- provider action descriptors for open, validate, execute, import, export, publish, inspect run/report, and hand off artifacts;\n- artifact ID handoff where Feedbax stays standalone with local refs but can accept/store Mandible artifact IDs when Mandible is present;\n- rebuildable index support for the new manifest kinds;\n- legacy/import adapters that can wrap older run/eval/figure records honestly, including uncertainty when provenance is incomplete;\n- extension-package registration depth for components, tasks, losses, analyses, report renderers, artifact codecs, and importers.\n\n## Design Constraints\n\n- Feedbax owns domain schemas, validation, registries, execution semantics, and emitted manifests.\n- Mandible owns provider registry, artifact store policy, provenance graph ingestion, reviewed provider actions, and cross-repo issue/session/auth graph.\n- Feedbax must remain usable without Mandible. Mandible enrichment should not become a required dependency.\n- Provider capabilities should be discoverable by agents without reading internal Python implementation details.\n- Durable runs that depend on unreviewed local code should be marked explicitly in manifests.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Provider manifest/capabilities expose eval, analysis, and report manifest/action surfaces.\n- Feedbax can emit or validate at least one evaluation manifest, one analysis manifest, and one report manifest shape with artifact refs.\n- The local index can rebuild/query those manifest kinds from on-disk manifests/artifacts.\n- Imported legacy records can be represented as best-effort manifests with explicit missing/uncertain provenance fields.\n- Mandible-facing handoff points are capability/schema based, not hardcoded Feedbax internals.\n- The implementation cross-links status back to `a3e46d5`, `c6c6da0`, `f68cf66`, and `e33f487`.\n\n## Related Issues\n\n- `a3e46d5` — product-depth and contract sequence umbrella.\n- `c6c6da0` — Feedbax manifests and provider contract.\n- `f68cf66` — Feedbax as Mandible provider/plugin.\n- `e33f487` — manifests as canonical lineage with database indexing.\n- `6a094c9` — Workspace runtime playback and validation overlays, which needs trajectory/eval artifacts.\n- `d90b3e5` — training runs vs sessions/tabs.\n- `e8452a4` — analysis-layer migration.\n- closed `fa3978f` — cross-repo roadmap ledger.\n\n---\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}